{"_id":"3vo6ClAX5KTHb7Sm","name":"Handy Haversack","type":"container","img":"icons/containers/bags/pack-simple-leather.webp","system":{"description":{"value":"<section class=\"infinity-item-description infinity-item-description--identified\" data-schema=\"infinity-dnd5e-description-state-v1\" data-identification-state=\"identified\" data-item-id=\"3vo6ClAX5KTHb7Sm\"><header class=\"infinity-item-state-header\"><p><strong>Identified State:</strong> Handy Haversack</p></header><div class=\"infinity-item-body\" data-content=\"rules\"><p><em>Wondrous item</em></p>\n<p>This backpack has a central pouch and two side pouches, each of which is an extradimensional space. Each side pouch can hold up to 20 pounds of material, not exceeding a volume of 2 cubic feet. The large central pouch can hold up to 8 cubic feet or 80 pounds of material. The backpack always weighs 5 pounds, regardless of its contents.</p>\n<p>Placing an object in the haversack follows the normal rules for interacting with objects. Retrieving an item from the haversack requires you to use an action. When you reach into the haversack for a specific item, the item is always magically on top.</p>\n<p>The haversack has a few limitations. If it is overloaded, or if a sharp object pierces it or tears it, the haversack ruptures and is destroyed. If the haversack is destroyed, its contents are lost forever, although an artifact always turns up again somewhere. If the haversack is turned inside out, its contents spill forth, unharmed, and the haversack must be put right before it can be used again. If a breathing creature is placed within the haversack, the creature can survive for up to 10 minutes, after which time it begins to suffocate.</p>\n<p>Placing the haversack inside an extradimensional space created by a bag of holding, portable hole, or similar item instantly destroys both items and opens a gate to the Astral Plane. The gate originates where the one item was placed inside the other. Any creature within 10 feet of the gate is sucked through it and deposited in a random location on the Astral Plane. The gate then closes. The gate is one-way only and can't be reopened.</p></div><aside class=\"infinity-item-state\" data-content=\"metadata\"><p><strong>Item State</strong></p><ul class=\"infinity-item-state-list\"><li>Container, Handy Haversack</li><li>Rarity: Rare</li><li>Value: 2,000 gp</li></ul></aside></section>","chat":"<p><strong>Handy Haversack</strong></p><p>Wondrous item This backpack has a central pouch and two side pouches, each of which is an extradimensional space. Each side pouch can hold up to 20 pounds of material, not excee...</p>"},"source":{"custom":"","book":"SRD 5.1","page":"","license":"CC-BY-4.0","revision":1,"rules":"2014"},"quantity":1,"weight":{"value":5,"units":"lb"},"price":{"value":2000,"denomination":"gp"},"attunement":"","equipped":false,"rarity":"rare","identified":true,"capacity":{"weight":{"value":120,"units":"lb"},"count":null,"volume":{"value":null,"units":"cubicFoot"}},"currency":{"cp":0,"sp":0,"ep":0,"gp":0,"pp":0},"unidentified":{"description":"<section class=\"infinity-item-description infinity-item-description--unidentified\" data-schema=\"infinity-dnd5e-description-state-v1\" data-identification-state=\"unidentified\" data-item-id=\"3vo6ClAX5KTHb7Sm\"><p><em>A handy haversack container awaiting identification.</em></p><p>This handy haversack container is described by stitching, wear, and fitted seams. Small details imply more value than a quick glance can confirm.</p><ul class=\"infinity-item-state-list\"><li>Visible form: Handy Haversack Container</li><li>Inspection cues: stitching, wear, and fitted seams</li><li>Identification state: Unidentified</li></ul></section>"},"container":null,"properties":["weightlessContents"],"identifier":"handy-haversack","attuned":false,"activities":{}},"effects":[],"folder":"uNQCicLJLwOY0FyO","flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.dnd5e.items.Item.7vqs5AqI4VCmuszx"},"dnd5e":{},"midi-qol":{"rollAtt