{"name":"Silk","type":"loot","system":{"description":{"value":"<section class=\"infinity-item-description infinity-item-description--identified\" data-schema=\"infinity-dnd5e-description-state-v1\" data-identification-state=\"identified\" data-item-id=\"PcXGYXebvqv0BS2z\"><header class=\"infinity-item-state-header\"><p><strong>Identified State:</strong> Silk</p></header><div class=\"infinity-item-body\" data-content=\"rules\"><p>A square yard of silk of average quality and weight. Used for all manner of items and clothing.</p>\n<p>The finest and most desirable of the common fabrics, silk is also the lightest. Most silks will weigh between 2 and 4 ounces per square yard. The heavier the silk, the higher the quality, more durable, and more opaque in color it is.</p></div><aside class=\"infinity-item-state\" data-content=\"metadata\"><p><strong>Item State</strong></p><ul class=\"infinity-item-state-list\"><li>Treasure</li><li>Value: 10 gp</li></ul></aside></section>","chat":"<p><strong>Silk</strong></p><p>A square yard of silk of average quality and weight. Used for all manner of items and clothing. The finest and most desirable of the common fabrics, silk is also the lightest. Mos...</p>"},"source":{"rules":"2014","revision":1},"quantity":1,"weight":{"value":0.2,"units":"lb"},"price":{"value":10,"denomination":"gp"},"rarity":"","identified":true,"identifier":"silk","unidentified":{"description":"<section class=\"infinity-item-description infinity-item-description--unidentified\" data-schema=\"infinity-dnd5e-description-state-v1\" data-identification-state=\"unidentified\" data-item-id=\"PcXGYXebvqv0BS2z\"><p><em>A trade good awaiting identification.</em></p><p>This trade good is described by stitching, wear, and fitted seams. Its practical use is apparent, but exact value and special details still need inspection.</p><ul class=\"infinity-item-state-list\"><li>Visible form: Trade Good</li><li>Inspection cues: stitching, wear, and fitted seams</li><li>Identification sta