{"_id":"34nuCCS4ZFkH0fth","name":"Spell Scroll: Sanctuary","type":"consumable","img":"icons/sundries/scrolls/scroll-bound-orange-tan.webp","system":{"description":{"value":"<section class=\"infinity-item-description infinity-item-description--identified\" data-schema=\"infinity-dnd5e-description-state-v1\" data-identification-state=\"identified\" data-item-id=\"34nuCCS4ZFkH0fth\"><header class=\"infinity-item-state-header\"><p><strong>Identified State:</strong> Spell Scroll: Sanctuary</p></header><div class=\"infinity-item-body\" data-content=\"rules\"><p>A spell scroll bears the words of a single spell, written in a mystical cipher. If the spell is on your class's spell list, you can read the scroll and cast its spell without providing any material components. Otherwise, the scroll is unintelligible. Casting the spell by reading the scroll requires the spell's normal casting time. Once the spell is cast, the words on the scroll fade, and it crumbles to dust.</p><p><strong>Stored Spell:</strong> Sanctuary (1st-level abj).</p><hr /><p>You ward a creature within range against attack. Until the spell ends, any creature who targets the warded creature with an attack or a harmful spell must first make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the creature must choose a new target or lose the attack or spell. This spell doesn't protect the warded creature from area effects, such as the explosion of a Fireball.</p><p>If the warded creature makes an attack or casts a spell that affects an enemy creature, this spell ends.</p></div><aside class=\"infinity-item-state\" data-content=\"metadata\"><p><strong>Item State</strong></p><ul class=\"infinity-item-state-list\"><li>Consumable, Scroll</li><li>Rarity: Common</li><li>Value: 60 gp</li><li>1 use(s)</li><li>Stored spell: Sanctuary</li></ul></aside></section>","chat":"<p><strong>Spell Scroll: Sanctuary</strong></p><p>A consumable spell scroll containing Sanctuary, a 1st-level spell.</p>"},"source":{"custom":"Infinity D&D5e genera