{"_id":"NzaTd8PKM4cB9qfT","name":"Spell Scroll: Haste","type":"consumable","img":"icons/sundries/scrolls/scroll-bound-gold-brown.webp","system":{"description":{"value":"<section class=\"infinity-item-description infinity-item-description--identified\" data-schema=\"infinity-dnd5e-description-state-v1\" data-identification-state=\"identified\" data-item-id=\"NzaTd8PKM4cB9qfT\"><header class=\"infinity-item-state-header\"><p><strong>Identified State:</strong> Spell Scroll: Haste</p></header><div class=\"infinity-item-body\" data-content=\"rules\"><p>A spell scroll bears the words of a single spell, written in a mystical cipher. If the spell is on your class's spell list, you can read the scroll and cast its spell without providing any material components. Otherwise, the scroll is unintelligible. Casting the spell by reading the scroll requires the spell's normal casting time. Once the spell is cast, the words on the scroll fade, and it crumbles to dust.</p><p><strong>Stored Spell:</strong> Haste (3rd-level trs).</p><hr /><p>Choose a willing creature that you can see within range. Until the spell ends, the target's speed is doubled, it gains a +2 bonus to AC, it has advantage on Dexterity Saving Throws, and it gains an additional action on each of its turns. That action can be used only to take the Attack (one weapon attack only), Dash, Disengage, Hide, or Use an Object action.</p><p>When the spell ends, the target can't move or take Actions until after its next turn, as a wave of lethargy sweeps over it.</p></div><aside class=\"infinity-item-state\" data-content=\"metadata\"><p><strong>Item State</strong></p><ul class=\"infinity-item-state-list\"><li>Consumable, Scroll</li><li>Rarity: Uncommon</li><li>Value: 200 gp</li><li>1 use(s)</li><li>Stored spell: Haste</li></ul></aside></section>","chat":"<p><strong>Spell Scroll: Haste</strong></p><p>A consumable spell scroll containing Haste, a 3rd-level spell.</p>"},"source":{"custom":"Infinity D&D5e generated spell scroll","