{"_id":"vwTPv23l9Ir89cok","name":"Spell Scroll: Conjure Woodland Beings","type":"consumable","img":"icons/sundries/scrolls/scroll-plain-red.webp","system":{"description":{"value":"<section class=\"infinity-item-description infinity-item-description--identified\" data-schema=\"infinity-dnd5e-description-state-v1\" data-identification-state=\"identified\" data-item-id=\"vwTPv23l9Ir89cok\"><header class=\"infinity-item-state-header\"><p><strong>Identified State:</strong> Spell Scroll: Conjure Woodland Beings</p></header><div class=\"infinity-item-body\" data-content=\"rules\"><p>A spell scroll bears the words of a single spell, written in a mystical cipher. If the spell is on your class's spell list, you can read the scroll and cast its spell without providing any material components. Otherwise, the scroll is unintelligible. Casting the spell by reading the scroll requires the spell's normal casting time. Once the spell is cast, the words on the scroll fade, and it crumbles to dust.</p><p><strong>Stored Spell:</strong> Conjure Woodland Beings (4th-level con).</p><hr /><p>You summon fey creatures that appear in unoccupied spaces that you can see within range. Choose one of the following options for what appears:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>One fey creature of challenge rating 2 or lower</li>\n<li>Two fey creatures of challenge rating 1 or lower</li>\n<li>Four fey creatures of challenge rating 1/2 or lower</li>\n<li>Eight fey creatures of challenge rating 1/4 or lower</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A summoned creature disappears when it drops to 0 hit points or when the spell ends.</p><p>The summoned creatures are friendly to you and your companions. Roll initiative for the summoned creatures as a group, which have their own turns. They obey any verbal commands that you issue to them (no action required by you). If you don't issue any commands to them, they defend themselves from hostile creatures, but otherwise take no actions.</p><p><strong>Higher Levels. </strong>When you cast this spell using certain higher-level spell slots, you choose one of the summoning options above, and more creatures appear: twice as many with a 6th-level slot and three times as many with an 8th-level slot.</p></div><aside class=\"infinity-item-state\" data-content=\"metadata\"><p><strong>Item State</strong></p><ul class=\"infinity-item-state-list\"><li>Consumable, Scroll</li><li>Rarity: Rare</li><li>Value: 320 gp</li><li>1 use(s)</li><li>Stored spell: Conjure Woodland Beings</li></ul></aside></section>","chat":"<p><strong>Spell Scroll: Conjure Woodland Beings</strong></p><p>A consumable spell scroll containing Conjure Woodland Beings, a 4th-level spell.</p>"},"source":{"custom":"Infinity D&D5e generated spell scroll","book":"SRD 5.1","page":"","license":"CC-BY-4.0","rules":"2014","revision":1},"quantity":1,"weight":{"value":0,"units":"lb"},"price":{"value":320,"denomination":"gp"},"attunement":"","equipped":false,"rarity":"rare","identified":true,"uses":{"max":"1","recovery":[],"autoDestroy":true,"spent":0},"damage":{"base":{"number":null,"denomination":null,"types":[],"custom":{"enabled":false},"scaling":{"number":1}},"replace":false},"unidentified":{"description":"<section class=\"infinity-item-description infinity-item-description--unidentified\" data-schema=\"infinity-dnd5e-description-state-v1\" data-identification-state=\"unidentified\" data-item-id=\"vwTPv23l9Ir89cok\"><p><em>A sealed scroll awaiting identification.</em></p><p>This sealed scroll is described by paper stock, ink, and binding. Its practical use is apparent, but exact value and spell formula still need inspection.</p><ul class=\"infinity-item-state-list\"><li>Visible form: Sealed Scroll</li><li>Inspection cues: paper stock, ink, and binding</li><li>Identification state: Unidentified</li></ul></section>"},"type":{"value":"scroll","subtype":""},"activities":{"dnd5eactivity000":{"_id":"dnd5eactivity000","type":"summon","activation":{"type":"action","value":1,"override":false,"condition":"Spell must be on the cast